Step #,Process Name,What Happens?
1,Load Original Record,Database se purana record uthaya jata hai (sirf Update ke case mein).
2,Load New Values,"User ne jo nayi values di hain, unhe purani values par overwrite kiya jata hai."
3,System Validation,"Salesforce basic cheezein check karta hai (Required fields, field formats, length)."
4,Before Record-Triggered Flow,"Sabse pehle ""Fast Field Updates"" wale flows chalte hain."
5,Before Triggers,Aapka Apex Before Insert ya Before Update trigger chalta hai.
6,Custom Validation Rules,"Aapne jo formulas banaye hain validation ke liye, wo yahan check hote hain."
7,Duplicate Rules,System check karta hai ki koi duplicate record toh nahi ban raha.
8,Save to Database,"Record save ho jata hai par ""Commit"" nahi hota. Is point par ID generate ho jati hai."
9,After Triggers,Apex After Insert ya After Update triggers yahan chalte hain.
10,Assignment Rules,Leads ya Cases ko unke sahi owners (users/queues) ko assign kiya jata hai.
11,Auto-Response Rules,Customer ko apne aap automatic response email bheja jata hai.
12,Workflow Rules,Purane workflow rules (agar koi active hain) yahan fire hote hain.
13,Workflow Field Updates,"Agar workflow ne field badli, toh Before aur After Triggers ek baar phir se chalte hain."
14,Escalation Rules,Case agar deadline mein solve nahi hua toh bade boss ke paas escalate hota hai.
15,After Record-Triggered Flow,"""Actions and Related Records"" wale flows yahan execute hote hain."
16,Entitlement Rules,Service Cloud ke agreements aur milestones check hote hain.
17,Roll-up Summary Fields,"Parent record par calculation update hoti hai (Count, Sum, Min, Max)."
18,Sharing Rules,Check hota hai ki record kis user ko dikhega aur kise nahi.
19,COMMIT,Sab kuch final ho gaya! Data permanent database mein lock ho jata hai.
20,Post-Commit Logic,"Commit ke baad Async jobs (Queueable, Future) aur Emails trigger hote hain."
